Issue #42 placeholder. This file exists so BUILD_RUN_MANIFEST can keep a
single, uniform input arity whether or not the GS panel lineage ran.

When `enable_gs_panel = false`, no GS panel manifest is produced, but a
Nextflow `path` input still requires a file (a process input cannot be
declared optional in Nextflow 26.04.6 -- `arity: '0..1'` is rejected for
inputs). This placeholder is staged in that case and never read: the
workflow passes `--no-gs-panel` to bin/build_run_manifest.py, which
records `"gs_panel": null` without opening any file. The flag is
explicit rather than inferred from a missing argument so that a wiring
mistake cannot quietly produce a manifest which understates what the run
actually did.
